When implementing authenticated client UI, lead outcome tracking, goals, revenue attribution, client dashboards, recommendations, client health, notifications, offers, package entitlements, or client reporting, read:

docs/30_VECTOR_CLIENT_EXPERIENCE_REVENUE_INTELLIGENCE_GROWTH_OUTCOMES.md

Authenticated screens use `docs/28` Control tokens. Public visitor UX stays `docs/27`. Creative production stays `docs/29`. Do not invent a third visual language.

Rules:
- Client UX is outcome-first, not infrastructure-first.
- Prefer simple business language.
- Use progressive disclosure. One Control app; nav differs by capability.
- Never imply attribution certainty when data is estimated or incomplete.
- AI must check data health before important recommendations.
- AI must not invent sales, revenue, close rates, or customer value.
- Marketing optimization should progress from traffic → lead → qualified lead → sale → revenue where data allows.
- Keep CRM, revenue, ads, and billing behind provider adapters.
- Every tenant-owned outcome must be client-scoped.
- Keep Phase 2 `lead_status` (`new | working | qualified | won | lost | spam`). Do not rewrite applied migrations.
- Extend Phase 1 `offers`; do not create a colliding second offers table.
- Money is integer minor units plus currency. Revenue amounts are optional.
